{\\mathrm{cl}},&d\\geq3.\n\\end{cases}$$K d​={K d one​,K d cl​,​d≤2,d≥3.​\n\nBy the stated duality, the same assertion also gives the optimal constants in the associated alternative kinetic-energy formulations. The conjecture is presented as the dual formulation of the Lieb–Thirring conjecture at $\\gamma=1$γ=1; the supplied text does not state a resolution of this formulation.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nLukas Schimmer, “The state of the Lieb–Thirring conjecture”, arXiv:2203.06051 (2022).\n\nkinetic-energy-inequalitieslieb-thirring-inequalityspectral-theory\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe state of the Lieb--Thirring conjecture - Science Explorer Abstract (https://scixplorer.org/abs/2022arXiv220306051S/abstract)\nciteturn4search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.7 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; ## The state of the Lieb--Thirring conjecture ... Publication  | eprint arXiv:2203.06051 ... Keywords  | Mathematical Physics Mathematics - Spectral Theory 35P15 81Q10\n\n## The state of the Lieb--Thirring conjecture\n\n### Authors\n\nSchimmer, Lukas\n\nEprint\n\n### Abstract\n\nIn 1976 Lieb and Thirring established upper bounds on sums of powers of the negative eigenvalues of a Schrödinger operator in terms of semiclassical phase-space integrals. Over the last 45 years the optimal constants in these inequalities, the values of which were conjectured by Lieb and Thirring, have been subject of intense investigations. We aim to review existing results.\n\n### Details\n\nPublication  | eprint arXiv:2203.06051\nPublication Date  | March 2022\nDOI  | 10.48550/arXiv.2203.06051\narXiv  | arXiv:2203.06051\nBibcode  | 